<title>RUSSIA: Russian 6-mth T-bill yield falls to 65.98 pct.</title>
<headline>Russian 6-mth T-bill yield falls to 65.98 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of six-month GKO discount Treasury bills fell to 65.98 percent at an auction on Wednesday from 82.62 percent at the previous auction on September 25, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast an average yield in the 68-75 percent range.</p>
<p>Full details of the issue follow:  </p>
<p>				    Oct 2		Sept 25</p>
<p>    Series number	     22052		22051</p>
<p>    Issue volume		8.50 trln rbls   7.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations	     1.00 million	   1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)	   11.28 trln	  6.81 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)	    6.61 trln	  6.32 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds		    4.70 trln	  4.11 trln</p>
<p>    Average price	    71.18 pct	  64.99 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price  71.00 pct	  62.00 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield	    65.98 pct	  82.62 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield 66.56 pct	  94.00 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			 224 days	   238 days</p>
<p>    Issue date		 Oct 2, 1996     Sept 25, 1996</p>
<p>    Maturity date	    May 14, 1997    May 21, 1997</p>
<p>Earlier the finance ministry raised 1.31 trillion roubles when it auctioned a new 1.50 trillion rouble tranche of three-month T-bills (series 21070), taking total proceeds from today's auctions to six trillion roubles.</p>
<p>The finance ministry also repaid about six trillion roubles in a maturing six-month T-bill (22027).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
